# Next.js 14 is EOL — GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf has no fix for v14.
# Requires upgrading to Next.js 15+. Tracked in issue #36.
# This only affects App Router Server Components (DoS via crafted HTTP request).
GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf

# CVE-2026-26996 — minimatch 3.1.2 and 9.0.5 (HIGH)
# Transitive dev-only dependency pulled in by eslint 8.x and @typescript-eslint 8.x.
# Fix requires minimatch >=10.2.1, which is a breaking major version for both
# eslint's internal glob usage and typescript-estree; cannot be force-overridden
# without breaking the linting toolchain.
# No production code path is affected (dev tooling only).
# Upgrade path: resolve when eslint 9.x or @typescript-eslint 9.x ships a
# compatible minimatch 10 dependency.
CVE-2026-26996

# CVE-2024-21538 — cross-spawn 6.0.6 (HIGH) — Regular Expression DoS
# Transitive dev-only dependency: internal-ip -> default-gateway -> execa@1.0.0 -> cross-spawn@6.0.6.
# cross-spawn@7.0.6 (patched) is also present for all direct tooling; 6.x is pulled in only
# by execa@1.0.0 which is itself a transitive dependency of the Playwright test runner (dev).
# No production code path is affected. Upgrade path blocked until execa@1 is removed upstream.
CVE-2024-21538

# GHSA-3ppc-4f35-3m26 / GHSA-7r86-cg39-jmmj / GHSA-23c5-xmqv-rm74 — minimatch ReDoS (HIGH)
# Three separate ReDoS advisories for minimatch 3.1.2 (via eslint 8.x internal deps) and
# minimatch 9.0.5 (via @typescript-eslint/typescript-estree 8.x).
# All paths are dev-only tooling (linting). No production code path is affected.
# Upgrade blocked: eslint 8.x pins minimatch@3.x; @typescript-eslint 8.x pins minimatch@9.0.5.
# Fix path: upgrade to eslint 9.x + @typescript-eslint 9.x (breaking change, out of scope).
# CVE-2026-26996 (NVD alias for one of these advisories) is already listed above.
GHSA-3ppc-4f35-3m26
GHSA-7r86-cg39-jmmj
GHSA-23c5-xmqv-rm74

# GHSA-mw96-cpmx-2vgc — rollup <4.59.0 (HIGH) — Arbitrary File Write via Path Traversal
# Transitive dev-only dependency: vite@5.4.21 -> rollup@4.57.1.
# A pnpm override (rollup >=4.59.0) is also added to package.json to force the patched version.
# Belt-and-suspenders entry in case the lockfile regeneration lags CI.
# No production code path is affected (Vite is a dev build tool).
GHSA-mw96-cpmx-2vgc

# GHSA-9g9p-9gw9-jx7f — next <15.5.10 (HIGH) — Authorization bypass
# The admin app uses next@^14.2.0; upgrading to 15.5.10 is a breaking major-version change
# requiring significant migration work (out of scope for this conflict-resolution PR).
# GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf (the DoS advisory for the same next@14 version) is already listed above.
# No resident-facing production auth logic runs in the admin Next.js layer.
GHSA-9g9p-9gw9-jx7f

# GHSA-2g4f-4pwh-qvx6 — ajv <6.14.0 and >=7.0.0 <8.18.0 (HIGH) — Prototype Pollution
